## Rules

- Never `print()`. Log with `from operonx.core.loggings import LOGGER`.
- Let names come from variables: `reply = chat(text=text)` is named `reply`.
  Write `name=` only when other code reads that name, and build one op per
  line.
- Branch with `if_(cond, a).else_(b)` inside the `>>` chain. Never build a
  `BranchOp` or `Branch` yourself.
- An op that raises does not raise: the run's result has `"$errors"`.
- No retry loop in an op (`[retry]`, guide page 06) and no "save progress"
  logic (`[durable]`, guide page 08).
- A run that is slow while its ops are fast: read its trace's metadata
  (`backlog`, `loop_lag_ms`, `cpu_pct`) before profiling. Guide page 08.
- To upgrade operonx: `{{upgrade}}`, then `{{run}}operonx guide`, then
  re-read `.operonx/guide/README.md`. After adding an operonx package
  (`{{add}} operonx-agents`), run `{{run}}operonx guide`.

